[2026-03-14T19:00:45.426Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QZJ4zn53xoKnrVbvYzW6Vh","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary report of the entire Google Flights app structure.\n\n## Google Flights App - Complete Exploration Report\n\n### 1. App Directory Information\n\n**App Name**: GoogleFlights\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n### 2. AppSpec.md Overview\n\nThe Google Flights Clone is a comprehensive flight search and booking application with the following pages:\n\n- **Search Page**: Main landing page with search form (trip type, passengers, cabin class, airports, dates)\n- **Search Results Page**: Displays filtered flight results with sorting options\n- **Flight Details/Booking Page**: Shows selected flight details and booking information\n- **My Trips Page**: Displays booked flights and tracked routes (Upcoming, Past, Tracked tabs)\n- **Explore Page**: Discovery page with map view, flexible dates grid, and deals\n\n**Color Scheme**: Google Blue (#1A73E8), light gray background (#F8F9FA), white surfaces, Material Design inspired\n\n### 3. Tests Documentation\n\nFull test specifications exist in `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md` covering all components with detailed test cases for:\n- TripTypeSelector\n- PassengerCountSelector\n- CabinClassSelector\n- AirportAutocomplete\n- DatePicker\n- SearchButton\n- RecentSearches\n- PopularDestinations\n- And more...\n\n### 4. AppStyle.md\n\nNo app-specific AppStyle.md exists. Styles are defined in component CSS files and global `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/index.css`\n\n### 5. Database Schema (scripts/schema.ts)\n\nComplete PostgreSQL schema with tables:\n- **airports**: IATA code, name, city, country, coordinates, timezone\n- **airlines**: IATA code, name, logo color\n- **flights**: Core flight data with departure/arrival times, duration, amenities\n- **flight_legs**: Individual legs of connecting flights\n- **prices**: Cabin class pricing (economy, premium_economy, business, first)\n- **sessions**: User session management\n- **recent_searches**: Search history per session\n- **bookings**: Booking records with reference numbers\n- **booking_passengers**: Passenger details per booking\n- **tracked_routes**: Price tracking for specific routes\n\nIncludes indices for performance optimization.\n\n### 6. Style Variables (src/index.css)\n\nCSS custom properties:\n- **Colors**: Primary (#1A73E8), hover (#1557B0), light variants, text colors, borders, shadows, error/success/warning\n- **Layout**: Sidebar widths (expanded: 240px, collapsed: 64px)\n- **Borders**: 4px, 8px, 16px, full radius\n- **Font**: Google Sans, Roboto, system fonts\n\n### 7. Redux Store Structure\n\n**Store Configuration** (`src/store.ts`):\n- Two main slices: `search` and `flights`\n\n**Search Slice** (`src/slices/searchSlice.ts`):\n- State: Trip type, passengers, cabin class, origin/destination airports, dates, recent searches, popular destinations\n- Actions: setTripType, setPassengers, setCabinClass, setOrigin, setDestination, swapAirports, setDepartureDate, setReturnDate\n- Async Thunks: fetchRecentSearches, saveRecentSearch, fetchPopularDestinations\n- Session management with localStorage token\n\n**Flights Slice** (`src/slices/flightsSlice.ts`):\n- State: Flight results, pagination, sorting, filters (stops, airlines, price range, duration, departure/arrival times)\n- Tracked route state\n- Actions: setSortBy, setStopsFilter, setAirlinesFilter, setPriceRange, setDurationRange, setDepartureTimeFilter, setArrivalTimeFilter, resetFilters\n- Async Thunks: searchFlights, loadMoreFlights, fetchFlightLegs, checkTrackedRoute, toggleTrackRoute\n\n### 8. Netlify Functions\n\n**db.ts**: Helper to initialize neon SQL connection\n\n**airports.ts**: GET endpoint for airport autocomplete with ILIKE search by name, city, or IATA code\n\n**search-flights.ts**: Flight search with pagination (20 results per page), filters by origin, destination, departure date, cabin class. Returns flight details with airline info, pricing, and leg count.\n\n**flight-legs.ts**: GET endpoint to fetch detailed legs for a specific flight (used for expandable details)\n\n**recent-searches.ts**: \n- GET: Retrieve user's recent searches from session\n- POST: Save new search with passenger counts, dates, cabin class\n- Session management via session token\n\n**popular-destinations.ts**: Hardcoded destinations (NRT, LHR, CDG, DXB, SIN, SYD, FCO, BKK) with minimum prices and gradient backgrounds\n\n**tracked-routes.ts**:\n- GET: Check if route is tracked or list all tracked routes\n- POST: Add a route to tracking\n- DELETE: Remove from tracking\n\n### 9. Component Files\n\n**Pages** (2):\n- **SearchPage.tsx**: Main landing page with search form and recommendations\n- **SearchResultsPage.tsx**: Results display with filters, sorting, and pagination (20 results)\n\n**Navigation**:\n- **Sidebar.tsx**: Collapsible navigation (Search, Explore, My Trips icons)\n\n**Search Components**:\n- **TripTypeSelector.tsx**: Custom dropdown (Round trip, One way, Multi-city)\n- **PassengerCountSelector.tsx**: +/- controls for adults, children, infants\n- **CabinClassSelector.tsx**: Custom dropdown (Economy, Premium Economy, Business, First)\n- **AirportAutocomplete.tsx**: Autocomplete with airport name, code, city, country display\n- **DatePicker.tsx**: Calendar picker with month navigation, disabled past dates\n- **SearchButton.tsx**: Validates inputs and initiates search\n- **SearchSummaryBar.tsx**: Editable inline search parameters with chips on results page\n\n**Results Components**:\n- **FilterSidebar.tsx**: \n  - Sort by dropdown (Best, Price, Duration, Departure time, Arrival time)\n  - Stops filter (Nonstop, 1 stop, 2+ stops)\n  - Airlines filter with flight counts\n  - Price range slider with histogram\n  - Duration range slider\n  - Departure/Arrival time filters (Morning, Afternoon, Evening, Night)\n  - RangeSlider subcomponent for price/duration\n\n- **FlightResultCard.tsx**: \n  - Airline logo (colored circle with initials)\n  - Departure → Arrival times with +1 day indicator\n  - Duration and stops info\n  - Price display\n  - CO2 emissions\n  - Expandable details showing flight legs with timeline, terminals, amenities, baggage\n  - \"Select flight\" button linking to booking page\n\n- **TrackPricesToggle.tsx**: Bell icon toggle for price tracking\n\n- **Pagination.tsx**: \"Load more results\" button\n\n**Home Page Components**:\n- **RecentSearches.tsx**: Displays up to 10 recent searches with route, dates, passenger count\n- **PopularDestinations.tsx**: Grid of 8 destinations with gradient images, price from display\n\n**Styling**: Each component has matching `.css` file with BEM-style naming\n\n### 10. Key Implementation Details\n\n**Session Management**: Uses localStorage to persist session token via `crypto.randomUUID()`\n\n**Form Validation**: Client-side validation in SearchButton with error states stored in Redux\n\n**Search Navigation**: URL parameters carry search criteria to results page\n\n**Flight Filtering**: Client-side filtering and sorting in SearchResultsPage component\n\n**Expandable Flight Details**: Lazy loads leg information from flight-legs API endpoint\n\n**Amenity Icons**: Uses emoji (📶 Wi-Fi, 🔌 Power, 🎬 Entertainment, 🧳 Baggage)\n\n**Data Formatting**: Helper functions for time display, duration, prices, airport labels\n\n**Accessibility**: data-testid attributes throughout for testing, semantic HTML\n\n**FlightSummary, PriceBreakdown, PassengerForm, BookingAction**: These components for the booking flow are NOT yet implemented (AppSpec describes them but implementation is not present in the codebase)\n\nAll files are located under `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/` with structure:\n- `/src/pages/` - Page components\n- `/src/components/` - Reusable components  \n- `/src/slices/` - Redux slices\n- `/netlify/functions/` - API endpoints\n- `/scripts/` - Database schema initialization\n- `/src/index.css` - Global styles"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ada89556e0a0a6e36 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 76281\ntool_uses: 39\nduration_ms: 101006</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67e5fc58-8ab1-425d-a7ae-dd3f15c6c632","uuid":"27eac668-699c-4674-b37c-3a05b89dcd9c","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the google-flights app under /repo/apps/. Find:\n1. The app directory name and list all files in it\n2. Read AppSpec.md\n3. Read docs/tests.md if it exists\n4. Read any AppStyle.md files (both apps/AppStyle.md and app-specific)\n5. Read AppRevisions.md if it exists\n6. Read any existing component files related to FlightSummary, PriceBreakdown, PassengerForm, BookingAction, and the Flight Details/Booking page\n7. Read the existing store, slices, and netlify functions\n8. Read scripts/schema.ts for the database schema\n9. Read src/index.css for style variables\n\nBe thorough - read all these files completely.","agentId":"ada89556e0a0a6e36","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary report of the entire Google Flights app structure.\n\n## Google Flights App - Complete Exploration Report\n\n### 1. App Directory Information\n\n**App Name**: GoogleFlights\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n### 2. AppSpec.md Overview\n\nThe Google Flights Clone is a comprehensive flight search and booking application with the following pages:\n\n- **Search Page**: Main landing page with search form (trip type, passengers, cabin class, airports, dates)\n- **Search Results Page**: Displays filtered flight results with sorting options\n- **Flight Details/Booking Page**: Shows selected flight details and booking information\n- **My Trips Page**: Displays booked flights and tracked routes (Upcoming, Past, Tracked tabs)\n- **Explore Page**: Discovery page with map view, flexible dates grid, and deals\n\n**Color S